course: dictionary
lesson: 5214
title: One word, many meanings: jaw
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. Jaw is a good example: it can mean a bone in your face, the mouth parts of an animal, or the gripping part of a tool.
explain: «Some of the fastest movements are tiny: a trap-jaw ant's jaws close faster than you could ever blink.» The word close tells you the jaws are moving, and the word ant tells you they belong to an animal. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Jaw can also be used in stories. «His jaw dropped» does not mean a bone fell out. The word dropped shows he was amazed, so jaw here means the lower part of his face, the part that opens when he is surprised.
fact: Jaw has more than one meaning: the bone that holds your teeth, the mouth parts of an animal, or the gripping part of a tool.
fact: The lower jaw is the only bone in your skull that moves when you eat or speak.
fact: «Jaws» usually means an animal's mouth parts, like a shark's or a crocodile's.
fact: «Jaw-dropping» means so amazing that it makes you stare with your mouth open.
fact: «In the jaws of danger» means very close to danger.
exercise: «Leopard seals are big hunters with powerful jaws and long teeth.» What are the jaws in this sentence? | The bones in a person's face | A kind of music | *The mouth parts of an animal | A tool that grips things
exercise: «His jaw dropped when he saw the goal.» What does this show? | He was hungry | He was cold | *He was very surprised | He was tired
exercise: «The jaws of the vice held the metal tight.» What do the jaws of a vice do? | *They grip things tightly | They make a loud sound | They chew food | They fall off the table
test: «A parrot's hooked beak and strong jaw crack hard nuts and seeds.» What does jaw mean here? | A kind of ant | A tool that grips | Something that is shut tight with pain | *One of the bones that hold the teeth
test: What does «jaw-dropping» mean? | Shut tight with pain | *So amazing it makes you stare | Very hungry | Boring and slow
exam: In «the grown-up teeth are packed into the jaw like eggs in a box», what does jaw mean? | *The bone that holds the teeth | Very surprised | The mouth of a shark | The grip of a pair of pliers
